/build/
*.user
.vs/

# Claude Code transient state. Only worktrees/ is ignored, so a project skill
# or a shared settings.json under .claude/ can still be committed deliberately.
.claude/worktrees/

# Build logs the IDE writes next to the specs it converts
build.log

# Scratch notes. The tracked backlogs (To Do.txt, Remaining Work.txt) stay
# tracked; these are personal working scratch.
why and what and to do.txt
More to do.txt
Manual and Auto Things To Do.txt
n.txt


# Packaging output (scripts/package_*.sh|ps1) and platform build trees.
dist/
build-linux/
build-mac/

# Visual Studio's "Open Folder" CMake support writes these itself: out/ is the
# build tree it configures into, and it generates both preset files rather than
# being given them. CMakePresets.json is normally a shared file that a project
# writes on purpose — this repository does not, so it is ignored with the rest.
# If a hand-written one is ever added, remove that line before committing it.
out/
CMakePresets.json
CMakeUserPresets.json

# The alignthree.com website: generator, templates, stylesheet and the pages it
# produces. The pages are uploaded by FTP rather than committed, and the site is
# kept out of the product repository entirely.
website/
